cmqmiv10p000j11yvkpd4ugbw	cmqmiuz9t000g11yv8lmqplsu	https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/100767769615786959925/reviews	Nicole Fors	1	Tasteless sauce, there were no spices at all but they claim basil and oregano go in the recipe but it tastes just like pure tomato sauce with tiny tomatoes. I looked at every piece, no spice. The crust was so thin it had bubbles and tasted like a cracker and some parts shattered and crumbled. Under the crust, I  saw these dots like a premade crust. I called and got the manager and once he heard I was upset gave the phone to the cook to explain this is how they do it. The manager would not say sorry or even offer me a partial refund. Literally, Little Ceasars stuffed crust and Dominos taste better. This chain has gotten so bad. They swear this is the official recipe. Just a cheese topped tomato cracker. And they said this crust was made that day. It is not good at all!	2026-01-25 01:16:12	\N	f	2026-06-20 15:38:07.465
cmqmilinc000911yv4sz9gqo4	cmqmilgw7000411yvgnrixmvf	https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/109744535089709809320/reviews	Kim Klimek	5	We loved our visit to Adelle’s in Wheaton. The atmosphere is warm and thoughtfully designed, the staff is kind and attentive, and the food is outstanding, elevated yet comforting. It’s a place where you feel both welcomed and taken care of. We will definitely be returning.\nCome for Happy Hour and stay for dinner!	2026-02-17 16:07:04	\N	f	2026-06-20 15:30:43.752
cmqmnlcmh00032lq4jdaq65mg	cmqmnlapq00002lq4hvgoisal	https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/116670443803533888833/reviews	Mary Pinski	5	Oh my gosh\nI love Gianni’s\nYou must try the Pear martini\nTheir bread is beyond compare. The olive oil “Italian butter” which I affectionately call goopy goop is addictive. So is the tomahawk pork chop.\nTheir menu offers so many choices. It’s made fresh!\nService is always fabulous. Oh my gosh!  The carrot cake was the best I’ve EVER had. And I’ve had a lot. We were able to split it three ways and I still took some home.\n\nThe ambiance feels like you are in Tuscany.\nI only wish they were open for lunch.\n\nI totally forgot to take pictures but I have provided some from their website. Sorry	2026-05-08 23:15:08	\N	f	2026-06-20 17:50:34.026
cmqmnlcq400052lq4nfy8mdx7	cmqmnlapq00002lq4hvgoisal	https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/102143571962654885840/reviews	Richard Montelbano	4	Chicken Parm was good, large portions of chicken. I got the Veal vesuvio.  Veal was flavorful and tender. Some of the potatoes were not fully cooked and still hard. Bread was crispy and fresh. Shrimp cocktail was good, but cocktail sauce needed more horseradish, not much flavor. I got the stuffed artichoke, nice and big, but way too much lemon. We got an order of meatballs to try. Meatballs were great, tasted like mom's Sunday meatballs, only larger. For desert we got the canoli.  Filling was very good, wrapped in a nice thin crust drizzled with chocolate syrup. In their defense, it was Valentines Day and very busy. I would go back again, but probably skip the appetizers.	2026-02-15 07:13:22	\N	f	2026-06-20 17:50:34.156
cmqmnlcs100072lq47uzqp7fo	cmqmnlapq00002lq4hvgoisal	https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/101871069069827423145/reviews	Kathleen Katrakis	5	We love this place.  This is our go to for good Italian food.  We like the pick your pasta, sauce and ingredients as well as the linguine vongole.  We are disappointed their sister location in Kildeer closed.  Service is always great as is the atmosphere.	2026-05-19 03:01:56	\N	f	2026-06-20 17:50:34.225
cmqmnlctv00092lq4gar5oedr	cmqmnlapq00002lq4hvgoisal	https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/109310662647388088057/reviews	Amy S	5	Gianni’s is one of our go to restaurants when dining out. The food and service is always top notch. Jennifer is our favorite server and absolutely a reason we keep coming back.\n\nOur only critique would be to add sound absorbing panels into the back room as it gets very loud and we prefer not to dine at the restaurant if we would be seated there.	2026-03-04 17:49:33	\N	f	2026-06-20 17:50:34.291
cmqmnlcvo000b2lq4ula0ut4y	cmqmnlapq00002lq4hvgoisal	https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/117393863783985478207/reviews	Montse Marques	5	I really wanted to leave an excellent review! My husband and I had dinner here to celebrate our nephew’s birthday. Everyone had been asking if I’d tried this restaurant before, and I finally did — I’m so glad I did!\nThe service was exceptional. Lia was our waitress, and she was amazingly sweet and provided wonderful service. The food was absolutely delicious — I even joked that I loved the water!\nWe also spoke with the manager on duty (I didn’t catch his name) to personally share our gratitude for the outstanding food and service. Overall, a fantastic experience from start to finish.\nI highly recommend this restaurant and we will be going back to enjoy it again!	2025-10-16 20:41:30	\N	f	2026-06-20 17:50:34.356
