cmqnpa11y000bi56cqqx65171	cmqnp9z0n0000i56cf9pd6f38	https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/108112283488955718222/reviews	Chelsea Villasana	1	Security is basically useless, some drunk dude pushed my sister and got in her face then my man had to step in so he wouldn’t try anything where was security? Not one in sight. It wasn’t just us with a problem with this guy either. When they did end up coming all the did was ask him to calm down and made us move a couple inches down with as packed as it is. Isn’t a lot. We also informed his group to please keep him in line but here I am having to write this down for other people, worst experience with security.	2024-11-28 06:59:31	\N	f	2026-06-21 11:25:31.223
cmqnzrrvu000178j8zoh2kba4	cmqmixd09000s11yvx1fbvpcb	https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/115754876744433863181/reviews	sarim mansoor	5	Want	2023-06-07 22:01:34	\N	f	2026-06-21 16:19:15.306
cmqmwio0y0009d942id997khg	cmqmvqr46000aa6oixvipltgh	https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/115216551966279526680/reviews	Kate	3	I've been to plenty of Korean saunas (when I lived in Korea) and I'd say that my experience at King Spa landed somewhere in the middle of these experiences.\n\nI only paid $32 to enter as I had a Groupon, so be sure to check on there because without the coupon it's a $75 entry fee which frankly, is a bit overpriced. The women's spa area was clean and refreshing, and most everyone was following the rules and keeping space. I do wish there were a few more pools to relax in (there are only four) but the ones that were there were nice. However, I felt they didn't keep the pools that hot and it would be nice if they listed the temperature of the pool next to it (as is common at pretty much all the jimjilbangs I went to in Korea). I didn't get a scrub so I can't comment on that. There weren't very many amenities provided, especially for the price. Only two hairdryers and no hairbrushes available. I brought my own comb and hairbrush and I would advise you do as well.\n\nThe sauna rooms were nice as well, however I didn't think any of them were kept that hot. I felt like they were a bit toned down and I definitely wish they were kept hotter, but that's a matter of personal taste I guess.\n\nI got the deluxe facial and I enjoyed the experience immensely. Sylvia did a fantastic job and I found the experience relaxing, however $220 is a bit on the steep side for the experience. I chalked it up to a new year's treat, but it wouldn't be something I would pay for regularly.\n\nThe second floor relaxation areas are probably the highlight of the facility. Multiple areas for lounging and all were kept quiet, and there's a few TVs to watch as well. None of the places I went to in Korea had lounge chairs this nice, so kudos to King Spa for keeping theirs nice. If you had an overnight layover and needed a place to sleep for a few hours, you definitely could here.\n\nNow for the cons:\n\n• The food is very overpriced for what you get. I got the spicy pork bibimbap and while it was good, for $20 I would expect a bigger portion or at least more side dishes. It didn't even come with kimchi or danmunji, which I would expect with bibimbap. The portion of gochujang was tiny as well. Plus the bottle of green tea I got was $8.99--an atrocious price for the portion. Unfortunately they can get away with charging these prices since you're trapped inside and are likely to get hungry during your time here, but the food really isn't worth the price.\n\n• While most people followed the rules, I do wish there would've been a bit more enforcement. There was someone in the nude spa area who was wearing skin color swim bottoms or underwear, which is explicitly not allowed (and affects the cleanliness of the spa). There was also someone in the steam room (in the nude spa area) who was using their phone, which is absolutely ridiculous in an area where people are naked and phones aren't allowed. I wasn't happy to see this and I wish the staff were a bit more proactive in enforcing some of these rules for safety and cleanliness.\n\n• I also was unhappy to see three kids in street clothes using one of the sauna rooms, considering street clothes aren't allowed in the facility passed the locker rooms. Multiple staff seemed to notice this and eventually an adult man came in to talk to them. It was then I realized that this man was the manager/owner, as afterwards one of the employees came up to him to ask a question. So it turns out if you are the owners kids you can get away with not following the rules. This really rubbed me the wrong way because it sets a bad precedent for everyone else, and I'd be surprised if such behavior was tolerated in Korea (where rule enforcement is saunas is INCREDIBLY strict).\n\n---\n\nOverall, my experience at King Spa wasn't bad. If you get one of the more expensive facials you get a coupon to come back for free, which unfortunately expires in one month. After that, you can use the coupon to pay for $22 admission, which isn't bad. I'll likely come back here to use the discount coupon, but I'll tailor my experience to try and maximize my $.	2026-01-01 06:46:26	\N	f	2026-06-20 22:00:25.378
cmqmwinvk0003d942fndmdz5z	cmqmvqr46000aa6oixvipltgh	https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/103426137497997187662/reviews	Daniel A GG	5	King Spa & Sauna in Chicago was an amazing experience. I spent my time in the men’s section and felt completely comfortable the whole time — very relaxed, respectful, and easygoing environment.\n\nThere are plenty of options to unwind — saunas, hot baths, cold plunge — and you can really take your time and just disconnect.\n\nI left feeling refreshed, lighter, and in a much better headspace. Definitely a place I’ll come back to. Highly recommend.	2026-03-29 19:48:03	\N	f	2026-06-20 22:00:25.184
cmqmilijq000711yvfudh9q7a	cmqmilgw7000411yvgnrixmvf	https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/107978694946773741084/reviews	Chelsea Beran	5	My husband and I worked with the incredible owners to host a private dinner in their banquet room after our small wedding ceremony. It was wonderful! Debbie was extraordinarily helpful, the food was delicious, the atmosphere was charming and beautiful, the staff was warm and friendly, and  the fees were absolutely unbeatable. We will come back often for anniversaries and date nights for sure!	2025-12-13 12:06:16	\N	f	2026-06-20 15:30:43.622
cmqmwins20001d942sodmmtdl	cmqmvqr46000aa6oixvipltgh	https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/115463009495298795774/reviews	Lomita Mom	2	Mid-experience.  Money grab experience.  Not stellar experience.  Pros:  clean.  Scrub was as expected. Note:  NO ENTRY AFTER 2 am to 6 am!\nPros:  soaking tubs aren’t “hot “ or “cold” enough.  $5.00 charge for “big” bath towels.\nServices are NOT 24 hours.  Services stop at 10 pm and food service stops at 9:15 pm.  ENTRY FEE at LEAST $40.00.  Tables aren’t comfortable (no face cutout so neck must be held in weird position when on stomach.) weird turn during scrub to wash hair!  Why not turn tables so patron doesn’t have to be turned naked on towel??? Masseuse TOO HARD!  Attempted to ask her to not be so hard but she ignored my requests.  I am so sore today on back, forehead, and face.  Maybe they could ask about pressure.\n\nEnded up costing over $400 for two people WITHOUT food.  Regularly go to one in my town where it’s 1/2 that price and everything is included for free including combs, razors,  toothbrush, towels!  I would expect more for free if charging entry fee!	2026-06-11 17:25:24	\N	f	2026-06-20 22:00:25.057
cmqmwinz50007d942pcycg8vb	cmqmvqr46000aa6oixvipltgh	https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/114711463670037265835/reviews	Ulyana T.	5	Great place to relax and recharge. My husband and I spent about six hours here and had a wonderful time enjoying the different saunas and calming atmosphere. It’s a perfect spot to unwind and escape from a busy day. We also tried the food and it was delicious, our favorite was the baked eggs. Overall a very enjoyable spa experience.	2026-03-19 20:53:29	\N	f	2026-06-20 22:00:25.314
cmqwnuh6h000d4sk4ko86a1as	cmqwnufsp000a4sk4ezqdwf9u	https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/111883776819474310205/reviews	Alexandria Shanklin	5	Such a beautiful restaurant with unique touches like glowing menus. The mocktails were great! The food was excellent. We really likes the salmon and key like crème brûlée	2026-05-18 15:07:56	\N	f	2026-06-27 17:55:21.594
cmqwnuh89000f4sk4yr9bklof	cmqwnufsp000a4sk4ezqdwf9u	https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/110782613256652643242/reviews	Laura Feller	3	The food was excellent & the space is simply beautiful. We came here for my birthday lunch and while it wasn’t busy, we found the service to be very minimal and the waitress was extremely hard to hear. It was a pricey for a lunch with no alcohol.	2026-04-18 21:14:01	\N	f	2026-06-27 17:55:21.658
cmqwnuha1000h4sk4qr486crd	cmqwnufsp000a4sk4ezqdwf9u	https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/107746430520695325573/reviews	David Michelotti	3	The food is just ok, it does not live up to the prices. We went on a Saturday night - service was very slow, we arrived for our reservation at 6:30 and did not leave until 2 hours later. The bus boys and waiters were loud communicating with each other in the service area, it was a bit chaotic. The atmosphere is very interesting there though with the church setting.\n\nThe ribs were not very good - below the bbq sauce there was no seasoning.	2025-11-02 04:26:43	\N	f	2026-06-27 17:55:21.721
cmqwnuhbu000j4sk4stclrs7c	cmqwnufsp000a4sk4ezqdwf9u	https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/104417788251596210888/reviews	D J	4	Very good place for a special location. It's a beautiful restaurant. We went there for birthday lunch. We ordered chicken pasta with a cream Creole sauce and the meatloaf. The meatloaf was a little dry. But a very large portion. The pasta was cooked well but the chicken was overcooked. I thought it was a little pricey. Give you fresh bread at the table. Overall, it was a nice experience. Service was decent. Bathrooms could probably be updated. There's a parking lot behind the building which made it convenient.	2025-10-23 14:57:39	\N	f	2026-06-27 17:55:21.786
cmqwnuhdl000l4sk47xh5y3r9	cmqwnufsp000a4sk4ezqdwf9u	https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/104388631004804738456/reviews	Linda Felde	5	There were 6 of us celebrating a birthday.  All of us loved our entrees.  Our server Mark V. was great.  He got each dish correct (as two of us asked for no red pepper flakes).  Highly recommend. Paradelle with lobster sauce was perfection.	2026-02-21 16:22:02	\N	f	2026-06-27 17:55:21.849
cmqmiv149000l11yvbcj6t4y4	cmqmiuz9t000g11yv8lmqplsu	https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/112560653364871855012/reviews	Misty Doane	5	Being New Yorkers (Upstate), we've had many kinds of New York slices all over the state and in NYC, so we thought, "When in Rome."\n\nWe sat outside on the most beautiful street, and there was plenty of shade. The service was great and the waitress even gave us a drink to go. The bathrooms were very clean and the atmosphere inside had cozy, little booths for four as well as larger booths for 6 - 8 people. There were plenty of larger tables, so seating would't be an issue.\n\nNow, the pizza... There were deep dish as well as "thin" crust, but even the thin crust wasn't New York thin. We chose the deep dish supreme with the sausage patty as the waitress recommended. The waitress served up our first piece and it was strange not to see cheese on the top. In my first bite, I could taste thick slices of fresh mushroom, thick red sauce (similar to a tomato paste), and a crunchy (not hard) crust. The crust was deep fried in the pan, similar to how Pizza Hut used to make theirs in the 80's. The crust tasted familiar...then it hit me. The crust tasted like the outside of a corndog, but not as sweet. The cheese was oozy, but it wasn't the main event. Everytime I took a fork full, I forgot there was no cheese on top to hold the toppings on, so it was a bit messy. The sausage patty that was exposed was a very mild, but huge slice of sausage that fit over the entire medium pie.    Unless you tried the sausage alone, you aren't able to taste it.\n\nAll in all, I was very pleased and would recommend this pizzeria to anyone!	2025-10-04 18:13:00	\N	f	2026-06-20 15:38:07.594
